From 378b490c475f2e8ce0290d2b91f147743eb9729b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:11:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] BoardWatch.release_gone also releases its -shm
 baseline fd

The checkpoint baseline reads each board's -shm through sqlite_safe_read's kept
pread descriptor. release_gone() closed the reader of a removed board but left
that descriptor pinning the deleted kanban.db-shm until the next
kanban_gone_board_handles.sweep().

Why it was missed: the sync loop always goes through sweep(), which already
calls release_unlinked_fds(), so the loop-level test passed; only the direct
BoardWatch contract test saw the leftover descriptor (required CI on
c78de9ca61, shard 4/12).

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_gone_board_handles.py::
test_watch_keeps_a_live_board_and_closes_only_the_removed_one is RED on
c78de9ca61 (one "kanban.db-shm (deleted)" descriptor) and GREEN here. The 84
test files that import the changed modules pass (3122 tests).

Lock safety is unchanged: release_unlinked_fds() closes only descriptors whose
inode has st_nlink == 0, the rule that module already applies in every sweep.

Hermes-Card: t_20097f02b6abaa50
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_board_watch.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_board_watch.py b/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_board_watch.py
index ab1a44dbc5..3a786a764e 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_board_watch.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_board_watch.py
@@ -176,6 +176,9 @@ class BoardWatch:
             gone = [key for key in self._conns if path_gone(key)]
             for key in gone:
                 self._drop(key)
+        if gone:  # the checkpoint baseline reads each board's -shm through a kept pread fd
+            from hermes_cli.sqlite_safe_read import release_unlinked_fds
+            release_unlinked_fds()
         return len(gone)
 
     def reset(self) -> None:
